<title>FINLAND: OUTOKUMPU TO EXPAND U.S. COPPER RANGE.</title>
<headline>OUTOKUMPU TO EXPAND U.S. COPPER RANGE.</headline>
<dateline>HELSINKI 1997-06-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>Finnish metals and mining group Outokumpu Oy said in a statement on Monday it would expand its copper alloy product range in the United States through a licensing agreement with Japanese Kobe Steel .</p>
<p>&quot;The deal gives Outokumpu the right to manufacture five different kinds of copper alloy strips developed by Kobe Steel for all purposes except semiconductor lead frames,&quot; it said, adding the alloys are KLF-5, KFC, KLF-5Z, CAC92 and KLF-7.</p>
<p>&quot;The deal will have a significant impact on Outokumpu Copper Kenosha's product range and also on its business operations in the automotive and electronics industries,&quot; Outokumpu said.</p>
<p>-- Helsinki Newsroom +358-9-680 50 242, news@reuters.fi</p>
